(
    lost_title: "NOVEMBER 10, 1975",
    lost_body: "AT ABOUT 7:20 P.M. THE EDMUND FITZGERALD WAS GONE FROM RADAR AND RADIO. NO DISTRESS CALL WAS MADE.\n\nTHE ARTHUR M. ANDERSON WENT BACK OUT TO SEARCH. THE WILLIAM CLAY FORD JOINED HER.\n\nWHAT HAPPENED IN THOSE LAST MINUTES IS STILL NOT KNOWN.",
    reached_title: "WHITEFISH BAY",
    reached_body: "THE LAND CLOSES AROUND YOU AND THE SEA GOES DOWN. YOU HAVE BROUGHT HER IN.\n\nTHIS ENDING NEVER HAPPENED. THE REAL SHIP LIES 17 MILES FROM THE ENTRANCE TO THIS BAY, AND ALL 29 OF HER CREW WERE LOST.",
    memorial_title: "THE 29",
    memorial_body: "THE EDMUND FITZGERALD LIES IN 530 FEET OF WATER AT 46 59' 54\" N, 85 06' 36\" W, IN TWO MAIN SECTIONS. THE 29 MEN ABOARD WERE NEVER RECOVERED.\n\nMARINERS' CHURCH IN DETROIT RANG ITS BELL 29 TIMES. THE SHIP'S BELL WAS RECOVERED IN 1995 AND IS AT THE GREAT LAKES SHIPWRECK MUSEUM, WHITEFISH POINT.\n\nTHE LOSS LED TO REQUIRED DEPTH FINDERS, SURVIVAL SUITS, BETTER CHARTS, REVISED WAVE FORECASTS, AND ANNUAL FALL COAST GUARD INSPECTIONS.",
)
